      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PRETTY MORSEL (10) gave a good sight when leading up at Naracoorte last start, finishing second, and was also solid when running on late for third here before that. She is overdue for her first win, and stepping up to 1600m for the first time could be the key to getting the job done. KHORASAN (8) has steadily improved with racing, and she made up some good late ground when finishing third here 10 days ago. She will also be trying a mile for the first time and can have the last say. OR AM I (9) has been a touch disappointing overall and will have the blinkers off for the first time here. She is backing up quickly and is definitely good enough to win a maiden race at short notice. BLABBER MOUTH (5) probably should have quit maidens by now, and she is resuming from a spell that would have done her the world of good. She also has the blinkers off for the first time and should be hitting the line hard. Each way. RED RIPPLES (3) is peaking at the right time and is worth including.",
